{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"4043256d8ce6767d09a8896b7cfac7be1fd34f002eccdb48cb1186fec9ec38fa","digest":{"component_or_area":"grounding metric backend","key_entities":["src/rebar/grounding/engine_b_backends.py::_metric_invoke","src/rebar/grounding/engine_b_backends.py::_scc_files","rebar.builtin.smell.metric-oversize","scc --by-file --format json","tests/unit/grounding/test_engine_b.py::test_metric_backend_requests_per_file_json_and_emits_only_over_cutoff","Files array","Code threshold 800"],"problem_keywords":["scc metric backend","per-file JSON","grounding detector","oversize LOC threshold","missing command flag"],"propositions":["_metric_invoke omits the --by-file flag when invoking scc, causing scc to return empty Files arrays in language summaries","_scc_files depends on per-file entries in the Files array and cannot yield results when the array is empty","the metric-oversize detector can never emit file matches above the 800-LOC cutoff because the threshold loop never executes against empty parsed entries","adding --by-file to the scc command invocation restores per-file entries and allows the metric threshold logic to produce documented matches","fail-open semantics for tool absence, nonzero exit, timeout, and invalid JSON remain unchanged by the fix"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787295038221215001,"uuid":"716674c8-2b0c-4b4d-86bb-00358a373762"}